(OPR-39 (undocumented precision): the logical operators carry the
 conventional precedence - `not` binds tighter than `and`, and `and`
 binds tighter than `or`. LANGUAGE.md:4875-4879 lists the three
 operators with no precedence at all.
 Line 1: `not denied and affirmed` fires, so `not` took only `denied`.
 Line 2: `not affirmed and affirmed` does not fire, confirming the same.
 Line 3: `denied and denied or affirmed` fires - false-or-true, so the
 `and` was evaluated first.
 Line 4: `affirmed or denied and denied` fires. Left to right it would
 be {true or false} and false, which is false; `and`-tighter gives
 true or {false and false}, which is true.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox OPR-39.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   not binds tighter than and
   and evaluated before or
   and binds tighter than or
)
a boolean called affirmed is true.
a boolean called denied is false.
If not denied and affirmed then, Print "not binds tighter than and".
If not affirmed and affirmed then, Print "not swallowed the whole conjunction".
If denied and denied or affirmed then, Print "and evaluated before or".
If affirmed or denied and denied then, Print "and binds tighter than or".
